<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Spain reckons with second deadly train crash of the year ahead of national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4939fcf894efbdcf1f38acf553c21dc40d541839dfa69b0dc2587648ab6d0f32</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:50:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-reckons-with-second-deadly-train-crash-of-the-year-ahead-of-national-election--79ed68a714bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-reckons-with-second-deadly-train-crash-of-the-year-ahead-of-national-election" /><summary type="html">Wednesday's deadly train crash has dealt a serious blow to Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez’s campaign. The accident in Toledo province killed 69 people and came just nine months after another deadly crash on the same line, leading to accusations from experts and the public of underinvestment in railway infrastructure under Sanchez's government after years of rapid network ​expansion.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump and Obama trade barbs in closing week of US midterm election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2823b8657a2073759236d83197c97a6396ad0764ff906102f0eb9535c483b17d</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:48:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-trump-and-obama-trade-barbs-in-closing-week-of-us-midterm-election--eced57ce1300.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-trump-and-obama-trade-barbs-in-closing-week-of-us-midterm-election" /><summary type="html">Neither man is on the ​ballot but Republican President Donald Trump and Democratic former President Barack Obama took prominent roles on the campaign trail on Wednesday, with less than a week to go before congressional races that could shift the balance of power in Washington. Thirty-five ‌of the 100 Senate seats and all 435 seats in the House of Representatives are being contested next Tuesday. Nonpartisan analysts generally favor Democrats' chances of capturing a majority in the ⁠House, with the contest for the Senate seen as very close.</summary></entry><entry><title>Minimum wage increase could come early as France braces for protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f6ec49e75f717392ad44fd66169673a31dab314cf4c39328bcc6cc8d8dc5c1e</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:47:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-minimum-wage-increase-could-come-early-as-france-braces-for-protests--72eb1a78a4e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-minimum-wage-increase-could-come-early-as-france-braces-for-protests" /><summary type="html">The French government is looking for new ways to calm social unrest ahead of more planned demonstrations over the cost of living this weekend. The minimum wage was set to increase on January 1, 2027. Now, officials are considering making the change one month earlier and adding an extra boost.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Real questions to be asked' after deadly train collision in Spain, journalist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8627435cf457edb6b8c2c12cfd86b8c5b7c044a997562c2d2936a37ec74a5b16</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:44:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261029-real-questions-to-be-asked-after-deadly-train-collision-in-spain-journalist-says--1490159b0812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261029-real-questions-to-be-asked-after-deadly-train-collision-in-spain-journalist-says" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we focus on the tragic train collision that killed at least 68 people in Spain on Wednesday. We're joined by Nicholas Kingsley, executive editor of Railway Gazette International.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Why is Donald Trump avoiding the Epstein case at all costs?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f723057ffd80fb6f99cd9719ed8dad87aba9183c8c89c91f33c5025c76e78d4a</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:37:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs--926236f51e51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs" /><summary type="html">The midterm elections campaign is in full swing in the United States, but Donald Trump is doing his utmost to avoid one subject: the Epstein Files. On January 30, the US Department of Justice published the court records relating to the Epstein case. At FRANCE 24, two of our journalists, Samia Metheni and Ava Luquet, delve into the 3 million documents to understand how Epstein's network operated. What did they find looking through the documents and what impact do they still have on Trump? Ava Luquet answered François Picard's questions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris becomes an open-air museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88baa567289a1644cdfdf6d20ea4816e0f44d7e8d7f420d167a1f3c5beb031ad</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:23:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261029-paris-becomes-an-open-air-museum--81116b859ca6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261029-paris-becomes-an-open-air-museum" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet David-Hervé Boutin, curator at "L'art dans la ville". He explores how the Getty Museum is bringing its collection to the streets of Paris. Masterpieces will be displayed on six of the city's façades, offering a unique open-air art experience throughout the French capital.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Putin seeks to expand ties with African countries at Russia-Africa summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:694d5c85d9dc802f6d5962e9df9c7ddaf558eba639d92ba77c90901889ecf88b</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:32:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit--7fe29c8b00d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday hosted dozens of African leaders at a Russia-Africa summit, part of Moscow’s efforts to expand its influence across the continent. The Russia-Africa summit marks a renewed Kremlin effort to bolster ties with a continent of nearly 1.6 billion people that is increasingly assertive on the global stage.</summary></entry><entry><title>DRC: C64 opposition coalition meets in Rome, calls for inclusive dialogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60fa0fe0edf2c52d5a926ffb67ea54aeaf9ee85acddee8fc743b55519d02d659</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue--2673a39bc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue" /><summary type="html">Democratic Republic ⁠of Congo's main ​opposition coalition, C64, met in Rome on Tuesday. Under pressure to respond to Joseph Kabila’s rebellion, its five leaders addressed the situation in the country from the Italian capital. They condemned any seizure of power by force and called for inclusive dialogue. FRANCE 24’s Emmet Livingston reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Trappes racist shooting suspect transferred to French court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae64ed8ee9fe576e243029e1efd2985c0f08aaebaf82b43a9a3e1c16867c5528</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-france-trappes-racist-shooting-suspect-transferred-to-french-court--154349787262.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-france-trappes-racist-shooting-suspect-transferred-to-french-court" /><summary type="html">French anti-terrorism prosecutor Olivier Christen said the suspect in the Trappes racist attack, which killed one person and injured five others, had been brought before a French court. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger: Guards accused of 'cruel, inhuman' treatment after 33 die in detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ab2ac9487d434c251f130589aceab8426660951a0981afc4df6aaa4d1ad2799</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:17:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention--06ca18f6c774.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention" /><summary type="html">In Niger, guards ignored the panicked cries for help from 33 detainees who died in a detention cell last month. Reports indicate that 72 people were crowded into a poorly ventilated, 20-square-metre space, where dozens slowly suffocated over 11 hours. The cell may have been cleaned and disinfected before it could be investigated. FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Very disturbing details': Trappes shooting suspect admits targeting victims by race, religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dc9a5b5e9bce586ec6cc6daffcdf4e3311f16e737a758c40908336d53410e2e</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:10:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-very-disturbing-details-trappes-shooting-suspect-admits-targeting-victims-by-race-religion--8ff667bcd1eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-very-disturbing-details-trappes-shooting-suspect-admits-targeting-victims-by-race-religion" /><summary type="html">A man suspected of a gun attack in the Paris suburbs last week that killed one person and wounded five including a child has admitted to "targeting individuals who appeared to be Muslim, African, or North African," prosecutors said on Thursday. FRANCE 24's Charli James reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain begins three days of mourning after train crash kills 69</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ba2a56e547adefd34533fe45059495e31bfdd375c5191dcc985360f794270f1</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:01:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-train-crash-kills-69--a6afb8b3d275.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-begins-three-days-of-mourning-after-train-crash-kills-69" /><summary type="html">Spain's second high-speed rail disaster this year, in which one train struck another from behind, killing 69 people, has raised fresh concerns about the safety of the country's rail network ahead of a national election. Three days of mourning have begun in the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis await final election results as difficult choices lie ahead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fad575f518b7af5893154b8e456850a4bffbc8ebdb7d49d99648747912f10af6</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:59:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-israelis-await-final-election-results-as-difficult-choices-lie-ahead--611940c40736.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-israelis-await-final-election-results-as-difficult-choices-lie-ahead" /><summary type="html">Israelis awaited the final election results on Thursday to confirm what appeared to be taking shape: neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his allies nor the array of parties seeking to oust him seemed likely to secure a majority of seats in parliament. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's train crash kills 69 people: What exactly happened?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8badadec31cd811471b19006d4766c571bebc4274e698b3672a2ed21a561109</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:53:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-s-train-crash-kills-69-people-what-exactly-happened--724a6701ea5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-spain-s-train-crash-kills-69-people-what-exactly-happened" /><summary type="html">In Spain, the deadly train accident that killed 69 people and injured scores has once again brought national railway safety under the spotlight. Spain’s transport minister reported an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to one of Europe's deadliest train disasters this century.</summary></entry><entry><title>US 2026: Georgia’s African Americans mobilise for the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb83cde36782d55b25535d229c333dbc88eea01bd6f936db12555538625d58d7</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:49:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-2026-georgia-s-african-americans-mobilise-for-the-midterms--344dcda86a4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-2026-georgia-s-african-americans-mobilise-for-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">This is one of the key states in the US midterms. In Georgia, Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff’s seat is on the line – and with it, perhaps, the Senate majority. African Americans, who make up around a third of Georgia’s electorate, are being urged to vote early.</summary></entry><entry><title>USA: Barack Obama slams Donald Trump in final midterm push</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f30e600eb4bca7ded2fcc47a56e73f68beba3327c78cc2b954678edbd1ce418d</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:28:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push--e90924907de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push" /><summary type="html">Just five days before the US midterm elections, former president Barack Obama came to Georgia in a show of support to Senator Jon Ossoff in tthe midterm elections. Obama commented on the reaction of Trump's administration to a joke he had made the day before. "He was very upset about the Cheesecake Factory comments", Obama said. "They mobilized a whole-of-government response to that joke. Not to inflation, but to that joke." As the election is getting closer, polls point to a possible Democratic majority in the House.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Feels like being hit by a bus': Rib remodelling beauty surgery on the rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:372c5d80a9b6b7fbe9984d47c840c8a3424ced6f2c19a765dd78b4b023fb3e77</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T11:54:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261029-feels-like-being-hit-by-a-bus-rib-remodelling-beauty-surgery-on-the-rise--30abf7734bd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261029-feels-like-being-hit-by-a-bus-rib-remodelling-beauty-surgery-on-the-rise" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 29: Spanish papers discuss Wednesday's deadly train collision. The New York Times investigates whether a "safest seat" in the event of a train crash exists. Next, we look at a report about "the shocking rise of rib remodelling". We end with some photos from the Arctic and Antarctica.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>At least 13 killed in 'horrific' Russian drone strike at Ukraine train station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6ee70b839463a03d76ab81d6cecd0a1350cc342ec767f63da8f228041e47f1c</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T11:36:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-at-least-13-killed-in-horrific-russian-drone-strike-at-ukraine-train-station--6f3d27577414.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261029-at-least-13-killed-in-horrific-russian-drone-strike-at-ukraine-train-station" /><summary type="html">At least 13 people were killed when a Russian drone struck a busy railway station in Ukraine's Dnipro on Thursday, President Volodymyr Zelensky said, describing the attack as "horrific" and urging Kyiv's allies not to ease sanctions on Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paris neighbourhoods: Exploring the lesser-known side of the 18th arrondissement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7113602c2dae3575cf8f78065d46c4b54771b0943bf1579427ffa7923ae0b481</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T11:30:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261029-paris-neighbourhoods-exploring-the-lesser-known-side-of-the-18th-arrondissement--14cc25ce38de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261029-paris-neighbourhoods-exploring-the-lesser-known-side-of-the-18th-arrondissement" /><summary type="html">In this edition of French Connections, Genie Godula and Florence Villeminot continue their tour of Paris with a stop in the 18th arrondissement. The district is famous for landmarks like the Sacré-Cœur Basilica and the Moulin Rouge, but in this show we step away from the picture-postcard version of Montmartre and take you to see the rest of the 18th. We visit the vibrant multicultural neighbourhood called the Goutte d'Or, then take you to the largest fabric store in the world and introduce you to some of the 18th's most famous residents over the years. Join us as we explore the lesser-known side of the 18th arrondissement.</summary><category term="French connections" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: French anti-terrorism prosecutor gives press conference on racist attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7528e6f111c31f14b211650aff58f0e094be4f8530e70ab33e8a9b22f6c41b94</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:56:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-replay-french-anti-terrorism-prosecutor-gives-press-conference-on-racist-attack--d3a956ca5cd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-replay-french-anti-terrorism-prosecutor-gives-press-conference-on-racist-attack" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor, Olivier Christen, gave a press conference on Thursday about the recent racist terrorist attack that killed one man and wounded five others, including a 12-year-old girl, in Trappes. Watch our replay.</summary></entry><entry><title>France reclaims title as Europe's champion of tax and social charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2e11666d21f90349d61106ef2ab3eed1b06395a4697d0f17e799a84f418321f</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:54:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261029-france-reclaims-title-as-europe-s-champion-of-tax-and-social-charges--e0c4144bde7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261029-france-reclaims-title-as-europe-s-champion-of-tax-and-social-charges" /><summary type="html">New data shows that France has the EU's highest tax burden at 46 percent of GDP, while its national debt continues to grow. Amid new street protests over lack of education funding and falling purchasing power, the government is proposing a meagre hike in the minimum wage. Also in this edition: US tech giants see their shares diverge as the AI boom pushes massive capital expenditures.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya's female athletes make their mark as Youth Olympic Games approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:548c5ca02f5f2c052f2725b68b5182741a8ea91f3eb37ecbf05b1ad2cf460474</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:45:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach--fa8c0d0a87ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach" /><summary type="html">Senegal is preparing to host the Youth Olympic Games, which begin this weekend. The young athletes who hope to showcase their talents on the international stage have their sights set on the Games, and Kenya has made sure that its young boxers remain on their toes and are ready to take on opponents of a higher calibre. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>'There's clearly a marketplace for Russian in Africa - but it's not about institution building'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2f93570fc039228488e53476815b1a9d9488daf79df7f1e2c488a91b94f108c</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:43:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-there-s-clearly-a-marketplace-for-russian-in-africa-but-it-s-not-about-institution-building--01b858d934fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-there-s-clearly-a-marketplace-for-russian-in-africa-but-it-s-not-about-institution-building" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Alex Vines, Africa Program Director at the European Council on Foreign Relations. He takes us through Russia's African paradox involving diplomatic Influence, security dependence and the politics of multipolarity. Moscow is gaining diplomatic traction across the continent even as its security partnerships, information operations and recruitment practices raise troubling questions about sovereignty, accountability and the human costs of geopolitical competition. For Vines, the participation of 48 African countries and 22 heads of state and government in the latest Russia-Africa summit illustrates the continuing appeal,  of Moscow as a diplomatic and strategic partner.</summary></entry><entry><title>Somalia: Lower house of parliament passes bill on sexual violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d549f17f427da4252f4ee89e1f02d1d7083bbdc118448d36511bbe723f6ae50</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:20:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence--471d5dd22da0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence" /><summary type="html">The Somali Parliament has passed a new law against sexual violence. The country’s criminal code dated back to 1962 and had not been updated since. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil met with Sofia Rajab in Nairobi. She is the program manager at the NGO Legal Action Worldwide, an organisation that lobbied Somali authorities in support of this new law.</summary></entry></feed>
